<!--
  Copyright (c) 2026 VitruvianSoftware
  SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

  What the screen.* tools are allowed to do, and what the user is shown before
  they allow it.

  canRetrieveWindowContent   - screen.tree. Without it rootInActiveWindow is
                               null and every read returns an empty screen.
  canPerformGestures         - screen.tap, long_press and swipe. Screenshots
                               and typing do not need it; taps do.
  flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows
                             - the OTHER windows: a dialog, the keyboard, the
                               second app on an unfolded foldable. Without it
                               screen.tree sees one window and reports a screen
                               that is missing the thing being asked about.
  flagReportViewIds          - the #view_id on each node. It is the one stable
                               handle across a screen that has been scrolled or
                               translated, so an agent can find the same button
                               twice.
  typeWindowStateChanged|typeWindowContentChanged
                             - the app reacts to neither, but a service that
                               subscribes to no events is not reliably given
                               window content on every Android version. They
                               are the price of the tree, not a feature.

  notificationTimeout is 100 ms so a burst of content changes is one delivery
  rather than hundreds while an app animates.

  The description is not marketing copy: it is the sentence on the Settings
  page that a person reads while deciding, and it has to name who gets the
  access (agents you have paired), what they can do (read the screen, tap,
  type, screenshot) and when (while the trust window is open).
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeWindowStateChanged|typeWindowContentChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagReportViewIds|flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows"
    android:canPerformGestures="true"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="true"
    android:description="@string/accessibility_description"
    android:notificationTimeout="100" />
